  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Stone is a block found underground in the Overworld or on the surface
    of mountains.\n\n<b>Natural generation</b>\nStone makes up the majority of the
    solid blocks generated in the Overworld above Y=0. From Y=8 downward, stone gradually
    transitions into deepslate, until it is completely replaced by deepslate at and
    below Y=0.\r\n\r\nWhen chunks generate, stone can be found under 1-5 layers of
    grass blocks, dirt, gravel, clay, coarse dirt, podzol, mycelium, sand, sandstone,
    red sand, red sandstone, or terracotta, depending on the biome. There is approximately
    11,520 stone per chunk.\r\n\r\nWhen the world is generating new chunks, some
    stone is replaced with ore features of other blocks. They may also be revealed
    on the side of small hills.\r\n\r\nStone also generates in igloo basements, some
    Overworld ruined portals, and in trail ruins. Stone also generates inside trial
    chambers with cobwebs on top next to trial spawners, indicating that the spawner
    is a spider or cave spider spawner. Stone can also generate in abandoned camps
    in dappled forests and meadows.\r\n\r\nStone also makes up most of the blocks
    on the void start platform in Superflat worlds created with the Void preset.
    \n\n<b>Post-generation</b>\nStone can also be made by lava flowing on top of
    water blocks (both flowing and source). The water is replaced by stone.\n\n<b>Breaking</b>\nStone
    can be mined using a pickaxe, in which case it drops cobblestone. When mined
    without a pickaxe, it drops nothing. If a stone is mined with a Silk Touch enchanted
    pickaxe, it drops itself.\n\n<b>Smelting</b>\nStone can be smelted from cobblestone.  "
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
